\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Sarah dialled Hayley, invited her to an immediate meeting, and almost suggested she bring her cutlass. In an atmosphere of Chip\'92s moodily generated smoke and gloom, Sarah waited dispassionately for Hayley to attend, taking her eyes from Chip for not a moment.\
Chip did not sit. The visitor chairs\'97deficient in both size and sturdiness\'97would not survive the luxury. He leaned casually on the only filing cabinet in the office in the same way a cement plant might lean on a bus shelter during an earthquake.\
Hayley arrived in four minutes.\
\'93Ah, Mr Stockwell,\'94 Hayley said.\
\'93Ma\'92am.\'94\
Hayley swivelled a chair so she could keep Chip in view while not appearing to disrespect Sarah\'92s presence, and sat.\
Both Hayley and Sarah waited Chip out in silence. It made him uncomfortable; he was used to people being in fear and awe around him, and he had spent his career in an organisation where nobody would shut up.\
\'93Five discs. Mr Damagetus,\'94 Chip started, naming Chilo formally. \'93Mr Damagetus wants a 
\f2\i pentagram
\f1\i0  of discs. What are we? A witch\'92s coven?\'94 He glanced at Hayley. \'93No offence ma\'92am.\'94\
Hayley let the apology slide, mostly because she had no idea what the tax it was about.\
\'93Have you any idea how crazy this is? You already know what happens when just one of these things spins too fast.\'94\
Sarah shuffled some papers on her desk, moved her computer mouse around and clicked a few times. Chip was in no position to see what was on the screen.\
\'93It seems that two discs proved to be more stable than one, correct? And they\'92re currently testing whether each could be spun at slower speeds for the same outcome?\'94\
\'93And what outcome would that be?\'94\
Sarah thought of the patterns in her dreams and shuddered. They\'92d only become more vivid as Little Clinton grew inside her. \'93Something or someone is trying to communicate with us, don\'92t you agree?\'94\
Chip put his tablet on the filing cabinet and then left it alone, because he had rehearsed with the tablet and understood that the moment he brought up a graph he would become a man with a graph. \'93You see patterns,\'94 he said. \'93I see weapons development.\'94\
Hayley sat forward and crossed her legs, and placed a finger to her lips. Chip scanned the room for where the listening devices and cameras might be.\
\'93Project Kebab is trying to clean up the signals we are already receiving, as well as looking for more. There are no plans to harness the disc\'92s instabilities, and all the evidence points towards using them in concert stabilises them.\'94\
\'93Fridge Force knows one thing,\'94 he said. \'93Sixty years of incident reports, and it comes down to a single line: stasis fields must never be allowed to interact with one another. It fits on a beer coaster. Two units in a building, you shield them. Two units in a room\'85 you don\'92t put two units in a room.\'94\
Sarah nodded slowly. \'93I hear you Mr Stockwell. And I need your continued expertise and vigilance. But let me assure you, we have not and will not develop the discs to blow shit up.\'94\
\'93Says the employee of an arms dealer,\'94 Chip replied.\
\'93All three of us are employed by Shakti Enterprises, Mr Stockwell,\'94 Hayley said while running her hand across her neck in a throat-cutting gesture. \'93And all three of us are committed to ensuring the safety of the research.\'94\
Chip tried another tack. \'93Mr Stoat wants five discs because a man with a beard recited him a poem.\'94\
\'93The Sages report to me,\'94 Sarah said, and then, slower: \'93All of Johnny\'92s reports, also report to me. And none of them have asked for three more discs.\'94\
Chip wanted to remind Sarah they all work for an arms dealer, but let his eyes drift to edges and corners of the room where bugs might be lurking. \'93Rotherhithe,\'94 he said.\
\'93You\'92ve said Rotherhithe before.\'94\
\'93The information is in the public domain. I suggest you study up on it.\'94\
Sarah dismissed the advice. \'93I already have studied up on it, Mr Stockwell.\'94\
Chip nodded slowly; he shouldn\'92t underestimate Sarah.
